What makes Mayport distinct is its setting — ocean on one side, river on the other, with the kind of humid Florida air that makes every deployment departure and homecoming feel like an event. The inlet is narrow, and ships transiting it navigate it carefully, a small drama that never quite gets routine.

Those who served at Mayport kept the Atlantic watch, and that work mattered.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('naval station great lakes', 'Naval Station Great Lakes', 'Naval Station Great Lakes sits on the western shore of Lake Michigan, about 35 miles north of Chicago, and its story begins in 1911 when the Navy established a permanent training facility on land donated by a coalition of local civic leaders determined to bring a naval presence to the Midwest. It was named for the great inland sea it borders — fitting, since it would go on to train more sailors than any other installation in the United States.

