For those who served or worked there, it was often unglamorous, demanding, and essential — the kind of place that kept the fleet ready so others could sail.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('puget sound naval shipyard', 'Puget Sound Naval Shipyard', 'Puget Sound Naval Shipyard sits on the western shore of Sinclair Inlet in Bremerton, Washington, established in 1891 as one of the Navy''s first facilities on the Pacific Coast. It was built to give the United States a capable repair and maintenance hub in the Pacific — a strategic necessity as American naval power began extending westward. The yard grew rapidly, and by the early twentieth century it had become one of the most important industrial installations the Navy operated anywhere.

