  ('newport news shipbuilding', 'Newport News Shipbuilding', 'Newport News Shipbuilding sits at the mouth of the James River in Virginia, where deep water and industrial ambition came together in 1886 when Collis P. Huntington founded the yard to build ships for a rapidly expanding nation. From the start, it was clear this was no ordinary facility — it would grow into one of the largest and most capable shipyards in the world.

