  ('electric boat (groton)', 'Electric Boat (Groton)', 'Electric Boat in Groton, Connecticut, is one of the most consequential addresses in American naval history. The company traces its roots to the late nineteenth century, when early submarine pioneers convinced the Navy that undersea warfare had a future — and Groton became the place where that future was built. For well over a century, the Thames River waterfront has been home to the design and construction of U.S. Navy submarines, from early diesel boats through the nuclear age.

