  ('hunters point naval shipyard', 'Hunters Point Naval Shipyard', 'Hunters Point Naval Shipyard occupies a peninsula jutting into San Francisco Bay, a site the Navy acquired during World War II to handle the enormous demands of the Pacific war. The location made geographic sense — deep water close to the shore, a natural drydock potential, and proximity to the industrial infrastructure of the Bay Area. The Navy expanded it rapidly into one of the largest ship repair facilities on the West Coast.

