  ('philadelphia naval shipyard', 'Philadelphia Naval Shipyard', 'Philadelphia Naval Shipyard carries one of the longest histories of any military installation in America. The yard traces its roots to 1801, making it among the earliest federal shipyards established by the young republic, built along the Delaware River where deep water and skilled labor made it a natural center for naval construction and repair.

