  ('charleston naval base', 'Charleston Naval Base', 'Charleston Naval Base traces its roots to the late nineteenth century, when the federal government recognized the city''s deep harbor and strategic position along the South Atlantic coast. The installation grew substantially during the World Wars, evolving from a modest yard into one of the East Coast''s most capable naval facilities. It was formally established as a major base in the early twentieth century and became a cornerstone of American sea power for decades.

