  ('naval base point loma', 'Naval Base Point Loma', 'Naval Base Point Loma occupies one of the most strategically commanding pieces of ground on the American coastline — a rugged peninsula guarding the entrance to San Diego Bay. The Navy established a significant presence here in the early twentieth century, drawn by the deep natural harbor and the peninsula''s elevation, which offered unobstructed sight lines across the Pacific approaches. The site''s history runs even deeper: the tip of Point Loma is where Juan Rodríguez Cabrillo made the first European landfall on the West Coast in 1542, making it ground that has watched over the Pacific for centuries.

