  ('nas jacksonville', 'NAS Jacksonville', 'Naval Air Station Jacksonville has stood watch over the St. Johns River since 1940, established as the Navy scrambled to expand its aviation training infrastructure ahead of America''s entry into World War II. The station was built on land that had once been a municipal airport, and it grew rapidly into one of the largest naval air training commands on the East Coast, turning out thousands of aviators and aircrew who would go on to serve across the Atlantic and Pacific theaters.

