  ('nas whidbey island', 'NAS Whidbey Island', 'NAS Whidbey Island traces its roots to 1941, when the Navy recognized that Puget Sound''s protected waters and the island''s natural geography made it an ideal site for seaplane and patrol operations on the Pacific coast. It was commissioned as a naval air station the following year, and its position in the Pacific Northwest placed it squarely in the defense of the American coastline during World War II.

