  ('nas lemoore', 'NAS Lemoore', 'Naval Air Station Lemoore sits in the broad, flat heart of California''s San Joaquin Valley, about 40 miles south of Fresno. The Navy chose this inland location deliberately — its distance from coastal fog and congested airspace made it ideal for jet operations. The station was commissioned in 1961, purpose-built from the ground up as a jet attack base at a moment when naval aviation was transforming around supersonic aircraft and nuclear strike missions.

