  ('nas fallon', 'NAS Fallon', 'Naval Air Station Fallon sits in the high desert of western Nevada, about sixty miles east of Reno, on land the Navy acquired during World War II when the military needed vast, unobstructed airspace for training. The station was commissioned in 1942 and has grown into the Navy''s premier tactical air warfare training center — the place where carrier aviators go to get serious before deployment.

