  ('lackland afb (jbsa)', 'Lackland AFB (JBSA)', 'Lackland Air Force Base traces its roots to the 1940s, when the Army Air Forces established it as a training annex adjacent to Kelly Field on San Antonio''s southwest side. It was named for Brigadier General Frank D. Lackland, a former Kelly Field commander who championed aviation training in its early years. When the Air Force became an independent service in 1947, Lackland grew into its own installation and took on a mission that would define it for generations.

