  ('nas jrb willow grove', 'NAS JRB Willow Grove', 'NAS JRB Willow Grove traces its roots to the early 1940s, when the Navy established a presence in southeastern Pennsylvania to support wartime training and East Coast air defense. The installation grew over the decades into one of the Reserve''s most important aviation hubs in the northeastern United States, named for the township it called home outside Philadelphia.

