  ('sheppard afb', 'Sheppard AFB', 'Sheppard Air Force Base sits on the rolling plains just north of Wichita Falls, Texas, a place where the wind comes in hard off the prairie and the sky stretches wide enough to humble anyone beneath it. The base was established in 1941 and named for Senator Morris Sheppard of Texas, a long-serving congressman who championed military preparedness and died in office just weeks before the installation bearing his name opened its gates.

