  ('luke afb', 'Luke AFB', 'Luke Air Force Base sits in the Sonoran Desert west of Phoenix, Arizona, on ground that has trained aviators since 1941. It was named for Second Lieutenant Frank Luke Jr., an Arizona-born World War I fighter ace who earned the Medal of Honor for destroying 18 enemy observation balloons and aircraft in just 18 days before being killed in action in September 1918 — one of the most aggressive combat records of that war.

