  ('creech afb', 'Creech AFB', 'Creech Air Force Base sits in the high Mojave Desert of Nevada, about 45 miles northwest of Las Vegas in Indian Springs Valley. The airfield traces its roots to World War II, when it opened as Indian Springs Air Force Auxiliary Field to support training operations at nearby Nellis. It was redesignated and renamed in 2005 to honor General Wilbur L. Creech, a legendary Tactical Air Command commander who transformed fighter aviation culture and readiness during the Cold War.

