  ('travis afb', 'Travis AFB', 'Travis Air Force Base sits in the Sacramento Valley at Fairfield, California, named for Brigadier General Robert F. Travis, who was killed there in August 1950 when a B-29 crashed shortly after takeoff. The base was established during World War II as Fairfield-Suisun Army Air Field, and it quickly became one of the most strategically positioned airfields on the Pacific Coast.

