  ('grand forks afb', 'Grand Forks AFB', 'Grand Forks Air Force Base sits on the flat Red River Valley plain of northeastern North Dakota, where the land runs open and wide in every direction. The base was established in 1955 during the early years of the Cold War, when the Air Force needed strategic bomber bases positioned in the northern tier to project power toward the Soviet Union. It was named for the nearby city of Grand Forks, which had supported military aviation in the region since World War II.

