  ('minot afb', 'Minot AFB', 'Minot Air Force Base sits on the high plains of north-central North Dakota, where the winters are brutal and the mission has always been dead serious. The base was established in 1957, named for the nearby city of Minot, and grew directly out of the Cold War imperative to put American strategic airpower within striking distance of any threat. It became one of the cornerstones of the nuclear deterrence mission that defined an era.

