  ('shaw afb', 'Shaw AFB', 'Shaw Air Force Base sits in the Sumter, South Carolina, lowcountry — flat pine country that has shaped generations of aviators. The base was established in 1941 and named for First Lieutenant Erwin David Shaw, a Sumter native and one of the first Americans killed in aerial combat during World War I. That heritage of early aviation sacrifice set the tone for everything that followed.

