  ('peterson space force base', 'Peterson Space Force Base', 'Peterson Space Force Base sits at the foot of Pikes Peak in Colorado Springs, Colorado, a setting that is equal parts dramatic and deliberate. The installation traces its origins to World War II, when it opened as a Army Air Forces field in 1942 and was later named for First Lieutenant Edward J. Peterson, a local pilot killed in a crash on the airfield that same year. The base grew alongside the Cold War''s demands, becoming a cornerstone of aerospace defense as the nation looked skyward for new threats.

