  ('presidio of san francisco', 'Presidio of San Francisco', 'The Presidio of San Francisco is one of the oldest continuously operated military posts in North America, founded by Spanish colonial forces in 1776 — the same year as American independence — to anchor Spain''s claim to the California coast. It passed to Mexico after independence, then to the United States following the Mexican-American War, and the U.S. Army established its formal presence there in 1846.

