Those who served at the Presidio stood on ground that four nations have called a military post — a remarkable testament to the enduring value of their watch.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('fort shafter', 'Fort Shafter', 'Fort Shafter sits on the western edge of Honolulu, Hawaii, and stands as the oldest active Army post in the Pacific. It was established in 1907 and named for General William Rufus Shafter, a veteran of the Civil War and the Spanish-American War who commanded U.S. forces during the capture of Santiago, Cuba in 1898.

