Today it remains home to U.S. Army Pacific, continuing a mission of regional engagement and readiness that spans from the West Coast to Asia. The historic buildings along Palm Circle, some dating to the territorial era, still stand in the Hawaiian heat.

Those who served here were part of something larger than any single conflict — a sustained American commitment to the Pacific that has lasted more than a century.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('fort wainwright', 'Fort Wainwright', 'Fort Wainwright sits on the edge of Fairbanks, Alaska, where the Chena River bends through boreal forest and the temperature can swing from 90 degrees in summer to minus 50 in winter. The post traces its roots to Ladd Field, established in 1940 as an Army Air Corps installation and a critical hub for the Alaska-Siberia ferry route — the ALSIB — that delivered thousands of aircraft to Soviet forces under Lend-Lease during World War II. It was redesignated Fort Wainwright in 1961, honoring General Jonathan M. Wainwright, who endured the fall of the Philippines and years as a prisoner of war before accepting Japan''s surrender alongside Douglas MacArthur.

