Those who served at Fort Greely earned their place on genuinely unforgiving ground, and the work they did there still matters today.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('anniston army depot', 'Anniston Army Depot', 'Anniston Army Depot sits in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains in northeastern Alabama, a place where industrial muscle and military precision have operated side by side for decades. The depot was established during World War II as the nation scrambled to build the logistical backbone needed to fight a two-front war. Its mission from the start was maintenance, overhaul, and storage — keeping weapons systems alive so soldiers in the field could fight.

