  ('tooele army depot', 'Tooele Army Depot', 'Tooele Army Depot sits in the high desert of northwestern Utah, about forty miles southwest of Salt Lake City, cradled between the Stansbury Mountains and the vast salt flats of the Great Basin. The depot was established in 1942 as the nation mobilized for World War II, built to store, maintain, and issue the enormous quantities of ammunition and conventional munitions that a global war demands. The surrounding desert — dry, isolated, and far from coastal vulnerability — made it ideal for that mission.

