  ('pine bluff arsenal', 'Pine Bluff Arsenal', 'Pine Bluff Arsenal sits in the Arkansas Delta, a flat, humid stretch of country where the Arkansas River bends south toward the Mississippi. The installation was established during World War II to meet the urgent need for chemical munitions production and storage, and it has carried that specialized mission ever since. Named for the city it borders rather than a person, the Arsenal became one of the Army''s principal facilities for the manufacture, storage, and later the destruction of chemical agents and smoke munitions.

