  ('blue grass army depot', 'Blue Grass Army Depot', 'Blue Grass Army Depot sits in the gently rolling farmland of central Kentucky near Richmond, established during World War II as part of the massive buildup of Army storage and logistics infrastructure across the American interior. Like similar depots created in that era, it was positioned inland for security and connected by rail to support the vast machinery of global war.

