  ('dover afb', 'Dover AFB', 'Dover Air Force Base sits on the flat, open landscape of central Delaware, a few miles from the city of Dover. The base traces its roots to 1941, when the Army Air Corps established an airfield there as the nation prepared for World War II. It was named after the surrounding city, itself one of the oldest in America. After the war, Dover transitioned to the newly independent Air Force and became a permanent installation in the airlift mission.

