  ('mather afb', 'Mather AFB', 'Mather Air Force Base sits on the eastern edge of Sacramento, California, on land that has served American airmen since 1918. It was established during World War I as an Army aviation training field and named for Carl Mather, a local aviator who died in a training accident — one of the earliest Americans to give his life to military flight. That sense of purpose in training would define the base for most of its history.

