  ('carswell afb (nas jrb fort worth)', 'Carswell AFB (NAS JRB Fort Worth)', 'Carswell Air Force Base traces its roots to 1942, when the Army Air Forces established a facility outside Fort Worth to support the massive expansion of American air power during World War II. It was renamed in 1948 to honor Major Horace Seaver Carswell Jr., a Fort Worth native and B-24 pilot who received the Medal of Honor posthumously for sacrificing his life to save his crew over the South China Sea in 1944.

