  ('bergstrom afb', 'Bergstrom AFB', 'Bergstrom Air Force Base traces its roots to World War II, when the Army Air Forces established a training field just southeast of Austin, Texas, in 1942. It was named for Captain John August Earl Bergstrom, an Austin native and the first Travis County servicemember killed in World War II, lost at Clark Field in the Philippines on December 8, 1941 — the day after Pearl Harbor.

