To everyone who flew out of Tustin or kept those aircraft ready to fly — your service shaped the Corps'' rotary-wing legacy.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('camp geiger / camp johnson (montford point)', 'Camp Geiger / Camp Johnson (Montford Point)', 'Camp Geiger sits on the southeastern edge of Marine Corps Base Camp Lejeune, North Carolina, established in the early 1940s to handle the enormous influx of Marines training for amphibious warfare in World War II. It was named for General Roy Geiger, one of the Corps'' most distinguished aviators and the only aviator ever to command a field army in combat. Over the decades it became home to the School of Infantry — East, where every Marine infantryman trained on the East Coast completes the Infantry Training Battalion course that turns a recruit into a rifleman.

