The land along the New River has shaped generations — infantry Marines, the first Black Marines, and everyone who followed in their boot prints.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('mclb barstow', 'MCLB Barstow', 'Marine Corps Logistics Base Barstow sits in the high Mojave Desert of California, about a hundred miles northeast of Los Angeles. The installation traces its roots to World War II, when the Marine Corps established a depot there to take advantage of the rail connections and the remote, arid terrain that was ideal for storing and maintaining equipment away from the vulnerable coast. It was formally designated a Marine Corps Logistics Base in the postwar years and has been a backbone of Marine sustainment ever since.

