The Mojave sets the character of this place — scorching summers, cold winters, and the kind of austere landscape that demands professionalism without ceremony.

To every Marine and sailor who kept the machines of war ready at Barstow, your work made the mission possible.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('mclb albany', 'MCLB Albany', 'Marine Corps Logistics Base Albany sits on ground in southwest Georgia that has supported American warfighters since World War II, when the Navy established a supply depot here to move material through the Southeast. The Marine Corps took it over in the postwar years, and it has been a cornerstone of Marine logistics ever since — receiving, rebuilding, storing, and shipping the equipment that keeps infantry and armor ready to fight.

