To every Marine and civilian who kept the machines running at Albany, your work made the mission possible.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('mcb hawaii (kaneohe bay)', 'MCB Hawaii (Kaneohe Bay)', 'Marine Corps Base Hawaii at Kaneohe Bay sits on the windward side of Oahu, a peninsula flanked by the Ko''olau Mountains and the deep blue of Kāne''ohe Bay — one of the more striking pieces of ground any Marine has ever been handed to call home.

The site''s military history begins before the Marines arrived. The Naval Air Station established here in the late 1930s was among the first installations attacked on December 7, 1941 — Japanese aircraft struck Kaneohe before the bombs fell on Pearl Harbor, and Navy patrol squadrons bore the brunt of that morning. After the war the base transitioned through several configurations before the Marine Corps took primary tenancy, and it has been a Marine installation in earnest since the early 1990s when forces consolidated from Oahu''s other sites.

