Those who served on that peninsula gave their time to one of the most consequential corners of the Pacific, and they did it with the professionalism the mission demanded.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('camp fuji', 'Camp Fuji', 'Camp Fuji sits at the foot of Japan''s most iconic mountain, and that setting is no accident. The Marine Corps established a presence here in the early 1950s, during the post-Korean War period, as U.S. forces needed reliable training ground in the Pacific. The installation sits in Shizuoka Prefecture, close enough to Mount Fuji that the volcano dominates the skyline on clear days — a backdrop unlike anything most Marines encounter anywhere else in the world.

