To every Marine and sailor who stood watch on that rugged northern shore — your service in one of the Pacific''s most consequential postings is remembered with respect.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('camp hansen (okinawa)', 'Camp Hansen (Okinawa)', 'Camp Hansen sits in the central highlands of Okinawa, part of the constellation of Marine Corps installations that have anchored American presence on the island since the end of World War II. It was established in the late 1950s and named for Staff Sergeant Dale M. Hansen, a Marine who earned the Medal of Honor on Okinawa in 1945 — fighting and dying on the very island the camp now calls home.

