  ('camp courtney (okinawa)', 'Camp Courtney (Okinawa)', 'Camp Courtney sits on the northeastern coast of Okinawa, overlookingKin Bay — a stretch of water that has witnessed American military presence since the island was secured in the summer of 1945 after one of the Pacific War''s longest and costliest battles. The camp is named for Navy Hospital Corpsman William E. Courtney, killed in action on Okinawa during that battle, one of many Navy corpsmen who gave their lives serving alongside Marines on that island.

