  ('camp kinser (okinawa)', 'Camp Kinser (Okinawa)', 'Camp Kinser sits on the southwestern coast of Okinawa, in the Urasoe area, and takes its name from Corporal Elbert Kinser, a Marine who was posthumously awarded the Medal of Honor for throwing himself on a grenade to save his fellow Marines during the Battle of Okinawa in May 1945. That act of selflessness is woven into the identity of the installation itself.

