Those who served at Camp Kinser kept the machine running — and that work matters every bit as much as the mission it enables.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('camp stanley', 'Camp Stanley', 'Camp Stanley, located near Boerne, Texas, in the Texas Hill Country northwest of San Antonio, traces its origins to the early twentieth century as an ammunition storage and testing facility. It was named for Captain Fielder A. Stanley, a U.S. Army officer killed in action during the Philippine-American War. The installation falls under the Army''s Joint Munitions Command and has long served as an ordnance depot — a place where weapons, ammunition, and equipment are stored, tested, and maintained rather than a traditional combat post.

