Those who served at Camp Stanley kept the arsenal ready — and that unglamorous, exacting work mattered more than most people will ever know.', 'claude-sonnet-4-6', true, now()),
  ('camp red cloud (uijeongbu)', 'Camp Red Cloud (Uijeongbu)', 'Camp Red Cloud sat on the edge of Uijeongbu, South Korea, a city whose name American soldiers knew well long before most of them were born. The installation was named for Corporal Mitchell Red Cloud Jr., a Ho-Chunk Nation veteran of World War II who was killed in action during the Korean War in November 1950 — holding his position against a Chinese assault so his unit could withdraw, an act that earned him the Medal of Honor posthumously.

