  ('camp walker / camp henry (daegu)', 'Camp Walker / Camp Henry (Daegu)', 'Camp Walker and Camp Henry sit in the heart of Daegu, South Korea, a pair of installations so closely linked they''ve long functioned as a single community. Camp Walker was established in the years following World War II and named for General Walton H. Walker, the Eighth Army commander killed in a jeep accident in Korea in December 1950 — a loss felt deeply across the peninsula. Camp Henry, adjacent and complementary, took its name from another American officer lost during the Korean War era, and together the two camps became the enduring home of U.S. Army Garrison Daegu.

