  ('k-16 seoul air base (seongnam)', 'K-16 Seoul Air Base (Seongnam)', 'K-16 sits on the southeastern edge of Seoul, on ground that has seen military aviation since the Japanese colonial period. The airfield was developed by American forces following liberation in 1945 and carried the designation K-16 during the Korean War, when the numbered K-site system organized airfields across the peninsula for rapid Allied use. Its location — close to the capital but separated from the city''s dense core by the Han River — made it strategically valuable from the earliest days of the conflict.

