  ('chinhae naval base', 'Chinhae Naval Base', 'Chinhae Naval Base sits at the southern tip of the Korean Peninsula, cradled by the mountains and quiet waters of Jinhae Bay. The site has served as a naval station since the Japanese colonial period in the early twentieth century, when its protected harbor made it a natural choice for maritime operations. After the Korean War, it became home to the Republic of Korea Navy headquarters, cementing its role as the most important naval installation on the peninsula.

