  ('hahn air base', 'Hahn Air Base', 'Hahn Air Base sits in the Hunsrück highlands of western Germany, a region of dense forest and rolling plateau that could feel remote even by Cold War standards. The base was built by the Luftwaffe in the 1930s and later occupied by American forces after World War II, eventually becoming a key installation in the United States Air Force''s European network. Its name derived from the nearby village of Hahn.

