  ('zweibruecken air base', 'Zweibruecken Air Base', 'Zweibrücken Air Base sits in the Rhineland-Palatinate region of southwestern Germany, a landscape of rolling hills and dense forest near the French border. The base was established by the United States Air Force in the early 1950s as NATO was building its forward defense posture in Western Europe during the Cold War. Its location — close to the inner German border and within striking distance of potential Warsaw Pact advances — made it a natural fit for tactical air power.

