  ('sembach air base', 'Sembach Air Base', 'Sembach Air Base sits in the Palatinate region of southwestern Germany, a few miles northeast of Kaiserslautern. The base traces its origins to World War II, when the Luftwaffe built the airfield in the early 1940s. American forces captured it in 1945 and eventually developed it into a permanent U.S. Air Force installation, one of a constellation of bases that anchored NATO''s Central European defense during the Cold War.

