  ('moron air base', 'Moron Air Base', 'Morón Air Base sits outside the city of Morón de la Frontera in Andalusia, southwestern Spain, a region whose mild climate and open skies made it naturally suited for aviation. The base traces its origins to the Spanish Air Force, but American involvement began in earnest in the 1950s under a bilateral defense agreement between the United States and Spain, when the Strategic Air Command established a presence there as part of its network of forward bases in Western Europe during the Cold War.

